From ab65a8167b304e56aa1603878136ecff9c340cfb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Haseeb Ashraf <haseeb.ashraf@siemens.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 03:24:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] venus: only reject legacy-tiled external images for
 scanout

vn_GetPhysicalDeviceImageFormatProperties2() rejects every external
image query with a tiling other than DRM_FORMAT_MODIFIER when the
renderer exports dma-buf, because venus does not support legacy
tiling for scanout. The check is not limited to scanout, so it also
rejects queries that only want to share an image between VkDevices
through OPAQUE_FD or dma-buf, even though the renderer supports them
and image creation, export and import already work for them.

Apply the check to the queries that can be used for scanout, the
ones chained with the mesa wsi hint, and forward all others to the
renderer so that it decides whether the combination is supported.
Common wsi chains the hint to the external image queries it makes,
the ones with DRM format modifiers, and its only other query has no
external memory info, so wsi behavior does not change.

An application that queries the dma-buf export of an optimally tiled
image without the hint now gets the answer of the renderer. The
layout of such an image is up to the renderer, so it is only
meaningful to share it with consumers of the same renderer.

Checked on an aarch64 host with a native NVIDIA 595.58.03 renderer:
OPAQUE_FD and dma-buf queries with OPTIMAL and LINEAR tiling are
supported. Through venus, an image exported from one VkDevice shows
the same data after it is imported into a second VkDevice.

Upstream-Status: Pending

Signed-off-by: Haseeb Ashraf <haseeb.ashraf@siemens.com>
---
 src/virtio/vulkan/vn_physical_device.c | 9 +++++++--
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/virtio/vulkan/vn_physical_device.c b/src/virtio/vulkan/vn_physical_device.c
index 6ac8437..0eebdf4 100644
--- a/src/virtio/vulkan/vn_physical_device.c
+++ b/src/virtio/vulkan/vn_physical_device.c
@@ -2730,8 +2730,13 @@ vn_GetPhysicalDeviceImageFormatProperties2(
          external_info->handleType !=
          VK_EXTERNAL_MEMORY_HANDLE_TYPE_ANDROID_HARDWARE_BUFFER_BIT_ANDROID);
 
-      /* venus doesn't support legacy tiling for scanout purpose */
-      if (renderer_handle_type ==
+      /* venus doesn't support legacy tiling for scanout purpose. Only the
+       * queries that can be used for scanout, i.e. the ones chained with
+       * the mesa wsi hint, are rejected here. For all other external
+       * images, leave it to the renderer to tell whether it can share them.
+       */
+      if (wsi_info &&
+          renderer_handle_type ==
              VK_EXTERNAL_MEMORY_HANDLE_TYPE_DMA_BUF_BIT_EXT &&
           pImageFormatInfo->tiling !=
              VK_IMAGE_TILING_DRM_FORMAT_MODIFIER_EXT) {
